.TH ADMIRAL\-INSTALL 1 "July 2026" "Admiral" "Admiral PaaS"
.SH NAME
admiral\-install \- bootstrap an Admiral platform node
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B admiral-install
\fB--single-node\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.P
.B admiral-install
\fB--dev-node\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.P
.B admiral-install
\fB--admin-node\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.P
.B admiral-install
\fB--admin-portal-node\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.P
.B admiral-install
\fB--worker-node\fR \fB--public-ip\fR \fIIP\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.P
.B admiral-install
\fB--portal-node\fR \fB--public-ip\fR \fIIP\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B admiral-install
provisions a fresh Enterprise Linux 10 host as an Admiral node. It selects the
Ansible playbook and security baseline based on the installation mode and
applies all required services, firewall rules, SELinux policy, WireGuard,
Podman rootless, and monitoring.
.P
The installer is idempotent for
.B \-\-single-node
and
.B \-\-admin-node
modes. Spoke modes
.RB ( \-\-worker-node ,
.BR \-\-portal-node )
revoke the bootstrap SSH key after onboarding; use
.B \-\-no-revoke-ssh-key
to preserve it for reconvergence.
.SH INSTALLATION MODES
.TP
\fB\-\-single-node\fR
All-in-one deployment. Installs admirald, admiral-fleet, admiralctl,
admiral-flagship, admiral-harbor, PostgreSQL, Caddy, and all supporting
services on a single host. Recommended for evaluation and small deployments.
.TP
\fB\-\-dev-node\fR
Single-node evaluation mode with relaxed security. WSGI servers are exposed
directly on ports 5000 and 5001. Cockpit is exposed on port 9090. Local
self-signed certificates are used. Not suitable for production.
.TP
\fB\-\-admin-node\fR
Control plane only. Installs admirald, admiralctl, PostgreSQL, WireGuard hub,
and supporting services. Does not install Caddy, flagship, or harbor.
.TP
\fB\-\-admin-portal-node\fR
Control plane and customer portal on one host. Installs all admin-node
components plus Caddy, admiral-flagship, and admiral-harbor. The typical
multi-node admin topology.
.TP
\fB\-\-worker-node\fR
Worker node for running customer workloads. Installs admiral-fleet, WireGuard
spoke, Podman rootless, and supporting services. Requires
.B \-\-public-ip
and a reachable admin node. Run this command from the admin node, which SSHs
into the target worker host.
.TP
\fB\-\-portal-node\fR
Standalone portal node. Installs admiral-harbor, WireGuard spoke, and
supporting services. Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-worker-node .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-public-ip\fR \fIIP\fR
Public IP address of the node being configured. Required for spoke modes
.RB ( \-\-worker-node ,
.BR \-\-portal-node ).
Optional for single-node and admin modes (defaults to detected IP).
.TP
\fB\-\-wireguard-ip\fR \fIIP\fR
WireGuard tunnel IP for a spoke node. Assigned from 10.99.0.0/24. If omitted,
the installer assigns the next available address via the admin hub.
.TP
\fB\-\-node-id\fR \fIID\fR
Custom node identifier. Defaults to the hostname. Must be unique within the
Admiral deployment.
.TP
\fB\-\-admin-endpoint\fR \fIURL\fR
Override the admin API endpoint that spokes use to connect. Detected
automatically in most topologies.
.TP
\fB\-\-ssh-user\fR \fIUSER\fR
SSH user for remote spoke bootstrap. Defaults to
.BR root .
During spoke installs the installer connects as this user, creates a dedicated
bootstrap account with NOPASSWD sudo, runs Ansible, then revokes the bootstrap
key and disables PermitRootLogin.
.TP
\fB\-\-ssh-key\fR \fIPATH\fR
SSH private key for remote spoke configuration. Defaults to the invoking
user\[cq]s default key.
.TP
\fB\-\-ssh-public-key\fR \fIPATH\fR
Public key to authorize for the generated administrator user on the target
node.
.TP
\fB\-\-ssh-fingerprint\fR \fISHA256:...\fR
Expected SSH host key fingerprint. The installer verifies this fingerprint
via ssh-keyscan before trusting the host. Strongly recommended for spoke
installs.
.TP
\fB\-\-s3-credentials-file\fR \fIPATH\fR
File containing ADMIRAL_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID and ADMIRAL_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY for
backup storage. Must be mode 0600.
.TP
\fB\-\-no-revoke-ssh-key\fR
Preserve the bootstrap SSH key after spoke onboarding. By default, the
installer revokes the operator\[cq]s SSH key from the bootstrap user and
disables PermitRootLogin after the Fleet\[en]Admirald handshake completes.
Use this flag when reconverging a spoke that already has a working
admiral-ssh identity, or when the handshake must be verified manually before
locking down root SSH access.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Confirm non-interactive dangerous operations such as
.BR \-\-dev-node .
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Display usage information and exit.
.SH BOOTSTRAP SSH FLOW
For spoke modes, the bootstrap SSH sequence is:
.P
1. SSH to target as
.B \-\-ssh-user
(default root) using
.BR \-\-ssh-key .
.P
2. Create a temporary bootstrap user with the operator\[cq]s public key and
NOPASSWD sudo.
.P
3. Verify the spoke node ID via
.B \-\-node-id
or remote role inspection.
.P
4. Run Ansible to install and configure all spoke services.
.P
5. Verify WireGuard handshake between hub and spoke.
.P
6. Verify the Fleet\[en]Admirald control-plane handshake via
.BR "admiralctl nodes ready" .
.P
7. Apply the security checklist (SELinux, firewall, auditd, fail2ban, etc.).
.P
8. Unless
.B \-\-no-revoke-ssh-key
was given, revoke the bootstrap SSH key from the bootstrap user and apply
PermitRootLogin no.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
Installation completed successfully.
.TP
1
A fatal error occurred. The installer prints a diagnostic message prefixed
with [FATAL].
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/admiral/role
Persisted node role. Written after first successful installation.
.TP
.I /etc/admiral/install.env
Installation state used to detect existing deployments.
.TP
.I /etc/admiral/secrets
Admiral secrets (mode 0600).
.TP
.I /etc/admirald.ini
Admirald configuration.
.TP
.I /etc/admiral/fleet.env
Fleet agent configuration.
.TP
.I /etc/admiral/harbor.env
Harbor portal configuration.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ADMIRAL_INSECURE_SKIP_VERIFY
Set to 1 to skip TLS certificate verification. Required on Fedora with
self-signed CAs due to strict OpenSSL 3.4 key usage validation. Do not use
in production.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR admiralctl (1),
.BR admiralctl-admin (8),
.BR admiral-install (8),
.BR harborctl (8)
.P
